#---
# purpose: "a guard naming an undefined name is rejected even in a clause nothing can reach"
# expect: diagnostic
#---
#
# # head_guard_pins_nothing_dead_clause
#
# The same undefined guard name as head_guard_pins_nothing, but behind a first
# clause that matches everything, so the guarded clause can never be selected.
# Pins are collected from every row before any of them is pruned, so a name
# that is bound nowhere is still a diagnostic. The alternative would let a
# reachability decision determine whether a program compiles.
def main() do
  dbg(dead(1, 0))
end

defp dead(a, _), do: :first
defp dead(_, y) when a > y, do: :other
